---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SKEPTICISM, ORG } from "../../../config";
---
<Base
  title={SKEPTICISM.name}
  description="The Center's program on what changes for people and organizations when the work starts being done alongside a machine. Convenings, research, and executive sessions."
>
  <header class="hband">
    <div class="hbwrap">
      <div class="hbtext">
        <h1>Co-Existing with AI.</h1>
        <p>Whether you are a student, an entrepreneur, or the leader of a business or a nation,
        you will need new strategies to become, and remain, successful.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hbimg">
        <img src="/images/hero-coexisting.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="1200" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="lede">
        Artificial intelligence is not arriving as a product decision. It is arriving as a change to
        what work is, who does it, and what a person is for inside an organization. Most of the
        material written about that change is produced by the companies selling the change. The Center
        works on the other side of it: what actually happens to people and institutions when the work
        starts being done alongside a machine, and what a leader is supposed to do about it on Monday.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead"><h2>What the program holds</h2></div>
      <div class="vgrid">
        <div>
          <h3>Coexistence is not acceptance.</h3>
          <p>Living alongside a technology means asking it to show its work before granting it trust.
          That is the ordinary standard applied to every institution, and the one artificial
          intelligence has mostly been exempted from. The Center holds itself to the same test.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>The question is older than the technology.</h3>
          <p>The Center has worked on how people and organizations coexist with automation since 2010,
          through robotics, through the last automation cycle, and now through this one. The through
          line is not the tool. It is what happens to the people standing next to it.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Written for the person who has to act.</h3>
          <p>Not for the reader who wants to be persuaded. Every session, assessment and paper is
          built to end in something a specific person can do, in an organization that already exists,
          with the constraints it already has.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead"><h2>From the program</h2></div>
      <div class="feat2">
        <div class="ft2a">
          <span class="mono">Microsoft Reactor Toronto · 20 February 2025</span>
          <h3>Coexisting with AI: Succeeding In the New Era</h3>
          <p>Created and hosted by Aseem Prakash, Founder and Chair, at CIBC Square. Part of the
          opening series at Microsoft Reactor Toronto.</p>
          <a class="pill pill--invert" href="/work/coexisting-with-ai/microsoft-reactor">The session &rsaquo;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="ft2b">
          <h4>Bring it to your organization.</h4>
          <p>The Center runs the session as a private briefing or a full-day workshop for leadership
          teams working out what changes in their own operation. Aseem Prakash delivers it.</p>
          <a class="pill pill--solid" href="/contact">Enquire &rsaquo;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead"><h2>How the program works</h2></div>
      <div class="appr">
        <div class="apfig" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 320 320" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <circle cx="160" cy="160" r="150" stroke="#111110" stroke-opacity=".1" />
            <circle cx="160" cy="160" r="112" stroke="#111110" stroke-opacity=".14" />
            <circle cx="160" cy="160" r="70" stroke="#DE3A11" stroke-opacity=".5" />
            <circle cx="160" cy="160" r="9" fill="#DE3A11" />
            <g stroke="#111110" stroke-opacity=".2">
              <path d="M160 10v40M160 270v40M10 160h40M270 160h40" />
            </g>
            <g fill="#111110" fill-opacity=".28">
              <circle cx="160" cy="48" r="6" /><circle cx="272" cy="160" r="6" /><circle cx="160" cy="272" r="6" />
            </g>
            <text x="160" y="30" text-anchor="middle" font-family="IBM Plex Mono, monospace" font-size="11" letter-spacing="1.6" fill="#8A877F">CONVENE</text>
            <text x="160" y="306" text-anchor="middle" font-family="IBM Plex Mono, monospace" font-size="11" letter-spacing="1.6" fill="#8A877F">PUBLISH</text>
            <text x="290" y="196" text-anchor="middle" font-family="IBM Plex Mono, monospace" font-size="11" letter-spacing="1.6" fill="#8A877F">ADVISE</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="aplist">
          <p class="apintro">The program runs on three motions, and each one feeds the next. What
          comes out of a room becomes something published, and what gets published is what an
          organization then pays the Center to help it act on.</p>
          <div class="ap">
            <h4>Convene.</h4>
            <p>Sessions that put researchers, policy staff and operators in the same room on the same
            question, rather than three rooms describing it to each other.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ap">
            <h4>Publish.</h4>
            <p>Assessments that let someone outside an institution measure it against a standard it did
            not set, and step-by-step material for the people who have to act on the result.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ap">
            <h4>Advise.</h4>
            <p>Private briefings and workshops for leadership teams, delivered by the Center's own
            principals. No client, sponsor or employer determines what the program publishes.</p>
          </div>
          <a class="pill pill--ghost" href="/contact">Work with the Center &rsaquo;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dark" style="padding:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 style="color:#fff;font-size:clamp(26px,3.3vw,40px);max-width:22ch">Host, partner, or bring
      the program in.</h2>
      <p class="attr" style="margin-top:22px;max-width:58ch">
        Host institutions shape the agenda alongside the Center rather than joining a finished one.
        Partners and organizations working on the same questions can write to
        <a href={"mailto:" + ORG.email} style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.5)">{ORG.email}</a>.
      </p>
      <a class="pill" href="/contact">Start a conversation &rsaquo;</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
